### How to use this file
#
# 1. Install the VS Code extension "REST Client" (humao.rest-client).
# 2. Get two tokens from the terminal:
#       npm run token 2            (a normal user)
#       npm run token 1 admin      (an admin)
# 3. Paste each token after the "=" signs just below.
# 4. Click "Send Request" above any request.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@userToken = PASTE_THE_"npm run token 2"_TOKEN_HERE
@adminToken = PASTE_THE_"npm run token 1 admin"_TOKEN_HERE


### Health check (no token needed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health


### User 2 views their own orders (newest first, default 20)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/2/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}


### Same, but 5 per page — copy "next_cursor" from the response into the next request
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/2/orders?limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}


### Next page — replace PASTE_CURSOR_HERE with the next_cursor value from above
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/2/orders?limit=5&cursor=PASTE_CURSOR_HERE
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}


### Admin can view any user's orders
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/2/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### User 2 tries to view user 3's orders -> 403 Forbidden
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/3/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}


### A user with no orders -> 200 with an empty list
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/21/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### No token -> 401 Unauthorized
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/2/orders
